1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,070
Got a shipping container landing in Auckland?

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:07,670
Here is how container devanning works at MOVe Highbrook in East Tāmaki.

3
00:00:09,204 --> 00:00:12,144
Devanning simply means unloading your goods from the container,

4
00:00:12,144 --> 00:00:13,624
checking them against your paperwork,

5
00:00:13,674 --> 00:00:15,434
and getting them ready for what comes next.

6
00:00:17,117 --> 00:00:19,257
How long it takes comes down to the container.

7
00:00:19,257 --> 00:00:21,547
Goods already on pallets come off with a forklift.

8
00:00:21,547 --> 00:00:25,257
Loose cartons, packed floor to roof, are unloaded and stacked by hand,

9
00:00:25,257 --> 00:00:26,267
so they take longer.

10
00:00:27,617 --> 00:00:30,917
Once your stock is off, it can be cross docked straight back out,

11
00:00:30,917 --> 00:00:32,807
picked and packed for your customers,

12
00:00:32,807 --> 00:00:35,317
or sent anywhere in New Zealand through the MOVe freight network.

13
00:00:36,784 --> 00:00:40,074
To book, or to get a time and a quote for your next container,

14
00:00:40,074 --> 00:00:41,654
call MOVe Highbrook.

15
00:00:41,664 --> 00:00:44,354
The full guide is at movelogistics.com

